@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-copy">
        <span class="page-kicker">About / data handling</span>
        <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="page-lede">Your camera data remains under your control.</p>
    </div>
</header>

<article class="prose">
    <span class="section-kicker">Local by design</span>
    <h2 class="h3 mt-0">No analytics, advertising, telemetry, or cloud storage.</h2>

    <h2 class="h4">Local data</h2>
    <p>Settings, frames, and videos are stored in <code>data/sessions</code>. Camera passwords are protected at rest with ASP.NET Core Data Protection.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Network</h2>
    <p>The app connects only to the camera endpoints you configure. It uses an anti-forgery cookie, not tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Deletion</h2>
    <p>Deleting a session removes its app-managed settings, frames, and videos. External backups may retain copies.</p>
</article>
